From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Oct 2026 15:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vga_switcheroo: keep the boot-GPU guard on non-T2 Apple

Patch 2009 ("apple-gmux: allow switching to igpu at probe") dropped the
"pdev != vga_default_device()" guard from vga_switcheroo_client_probe_defer()
so that on T2 Macs BOTH GPUs wait for the gmux before probing and the switch
to the iGPU can happen at probe time.

The guard, however, is what protected a machine whose APP000B (gmux) ACPI
device exists but whose gmux is NOT functional.  apple_gmux_present() is only

    acpi_dev_found("APP000B")

so it is true even when apple-gmux's own apple_gmux_detect() later fails and
gmux_probe() returns -ENODEV ("gmux device not present").  In that case no
vga_switcheroo handler is ever registered, vgasr_priv.handler_flags stays 0,
and with patch 2009 the sole/boot GPU is:

    vga_switcheroo_client_probe_defer() -> true
    i915_pci_probe()                    -> -EPROBE_DEFER (-517)
    ... forever (no handler can ever appear)

User-visible symptom: the machine boots, ssh works, but there is no /dev/dri
and no /sys/class/drm/card*, so greetd's ExecCondition
(/usr/local/bin/ncz-has-drm-output) fails and the greeter is skipped -- headless
with no error.  Reproduced on Macmini5,1 (2011, Sandy Bridge HD 3000, ACPI
APP000B present, in-kernel apple_gmux fails to bind).  It is NOT a generic
Sandy Bridge problem: non-Apple machines do not expose APP000B, and T2 Macs'
gmux (apple-gmux, or t2gmux from cix-installer post-install/56-t2-dkms.sh) does
register a handler, so the deferral there resolves.

Fix: keep the patch-2009 relaxation only where a handler really does arrive
(T2, identified by the Apple T2 bridge PCI device 106b:1801 every T2 Mac has
before the GPU drivers probe); everywhere else restore the upstream boot-GPU
guard.  Non-T2 dual-GPU Macs with a working gmux are unaffected: their inactive
GPU still defers exactly as upstream, and the boot GPU probes immediately as
upstream.

Fixes: 2009-apple-gmux-allow-switching-to-igpu-at-probe.patch
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/vga/vga_switcheroo.c | 19 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/vga/vga_switcheroo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/vga/vga_switcheroo.c
@@ -420,6 +420,25 @@
 		if (client->active)
 			return client;
 	return NULL;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Apple firmware advertises the APP000B (gmux) ACPI device on machines whose
+ * gmux is not functional (e.g. the single-GPU Macmini5,1).  There
+ * apple_gmux_present() is true -- it is only acpi_dev_found("APP000B") -- but
+ * apple-gmux's probe fails, so no vga_switcheroo handler is ever registered.
+ * The Apple T2 bridge is the reliable "a handler really does arrive" signal
+ * for the machines the relaxed defer below was added for.
+ */
+static bool apple_t2_present(void)
+{
+	struct pci_dev *pdev;
+
+	pdev = pci_get_device(PCI_VENDOR_ID_APPLE, 0x1801, NULL);
+	if (!pdev)
+		return false;
+	pci_dev_put(pdev);
+	return true;
 }
 
 /**
@@ -436,7 +455,20 @@
 bool vga_switcheroo_client_probe_defer(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 {
 	if (pci_is_display(pdev)) {
-		if (apple_gmux_present() && !vgasr_priv.handler_flags)
+		/*
+		 * apple-gmux is needed on pre-retina MacBook Pro to probe the
+		 * panel if pdev is the inactive GPU.
+		 *
+		 * On the T2 Macs this relaxation was added for, the gmux
+		 * handler really does register, so both GPUs may wait for it.
+		 * Elsewhere keep the upstream guard: a present-but-dead APP000B
+		 * (behind which no handler ever appears) must not starve the
+		 * boot GPU.  Without it i915 defers forever on e.g. Macmini5,1
+		 * -- no /dev/dri, no DRM connector, greetd skipped: headless
+		 * with no error.
+		 */
+		if (apple_gmux_present() && !vgasr_priv.handler_flags &&
+		    (pdev != vga_default_device() || apple_t2_present()))
 			return true;
 	}
 
